--------------------------------------------------------------------------
A note on what this licence does and does not cover
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT licence above covers the code and the documentation in this
repository.

It does not and cannot cover the texts this software retrieves. Those carry
their own licences, which the tool reports rather than assumes:

  Sefaria          per-edition; the API returns a `license` field for every
                   version, and this tool surfaces it rather than hiding it.
  Hebcal           CC-BY-4.0, attribution required.
  PocketTorah      CC-BY-SA, attribution required.

Neither does it cover the published romanization standards in `sources/`.
Those PDFs are not committed. Two of the five are copyrighted commercial
publications, and `sources/manifest.md` records where each one came from and
what its rights status is.

What is committed is the table data extracted from those standards, in
`schemes/`. A table of romanization correspondences is a set of facts about
how one writing system maps onto another, and facts are not protectable
expression.
